  "term": "association-reaction time",
  "definition": "Association-reaction time is the reaction interval in a task where a spoken word starts a chain of associations, and the person then makes an agreed motor response after that associative process is finished. It is a more complex form of reaction time than a simple reflex-like response because it includes the time taken by the central associative process.",
